Z||000002||HYPTNOTiSE||08-03-2000||02:05 AM||||Damn that's bad ass! Joe wynman did a similar setup, and if i do a v-8 swap i think i'd do the same. I'm curious about the reverse rotation. After my car is finished i'm going to build a fiero stricktly drag car. What do you think about a 454BB chevy? The only reason is cos i have access to a bad ass one cheap.  I was thinking of using either a stroked 350 or a destroked 400. Partly cos i have access to the destroked 400 cheap.  a 383 would be bad ass. I want it to be carbed and 12:1. With mucho nitrous. Are the toranado tranny's fairly stout? Would you do standart rotation or reverse for a strictly drag car?  Let me know your ideas.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
